@startuml magic-link-signup
' Spec 001 — sign up and first login via magic link (REQ-001-2, REQ-001-3).
' Parties: Browser, JairojobsWeb (LiveView), Jairojobs.Accounts, Mailer, user's inbox.

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Visitor
participant "Browser" as B
participant "JairojobsWeb\n(LiveView)" as W
participant "Jairojobs.Accounts" as ACC
database "Postgres" as DB
participant "Jairojobs.Mailer\n(Swoosh)" as M
participant "Visitor's inbox" as INBOX

== Sign up ==
Visitor -> B : open /users/register
B -> W : mount
W --> B : form (email, role)
Visitor -> B : submit email + role
B -> W : submit
W -> ACC : register_user(%{email, role})
ACC -> DB : insert user\n(confirmed_at: nil, role)
alt new email
  DB --> ACC : {:ok, user}
  ACC -> ACC : build login token\n(hashed, expires 15 min)
  ACC -> DB : insert user_token
  ACC -> M : deliver_login_instructions(user, url)
  M -> INBOX : email with magic link
else email already registered
  DB --> ACC : unique violation
  note right of ACC : no email sent, no duplicate
end
ACC --> W : {:ok, ...}
W --> B : neutral message:\n"If your email is in our system,\nyou'll receive instructions"

== Confirm + first login ==
Visitor -> INBOX : open email
INBOX -> B : click link /users/log-in/:token
B -> W : GET with token
W -> ACC : login_user_by_magic_link(token)
ACC -> DB : lookup token (hash),\ncheck expiry
alt valid, unused, user unconfirmed
  ACC -> DB : set confirmed_at = now
  ACC -> DB : delete ALL tokens for user
  note right of ACC : revoking everything on first\nconfirmation blocks pre-stuffing
  ACC --> W : {:ok, user}
  W -> W : create session token
  W --> B : redirect, logged in
else expired / used / unknown
  ACC --> W : :error
  W --> B : "link is invalid or expired"
end

== Later logins ==
note over B, INBOX
  Same flow from /users/log-in without the sign-up step.
  Once a password is set in Settings, email + password login is also accepted
  (REQ-001-5). Unconfirmed users are always refused (REQ-001-3).
end note

@enduml
